| NumPy negative control, one thread | {{ sx(h ~ "numpy.geomean.t1") }} |

A speed-up is the baseline median divided by the candidate median, with a
ninety-five percent percentile-bootstrap interval. **When the interval includes
parity this page says "no measurable difference", whatever the point estimate.**

## How much can COOL help this pipeline? (Amdahl bound)

COOL accelerates only KleidiCV-listed operations. The call census measures what
share of the pipeline's time those operations take on the baseline arm; the
report turns that share into the largest speed-up COOL could deliver even if
every listed operation became free, and into a prediction from the measured
per-group speed-ups.

{% set amodes = [] %}
{% for name in metrics(B, "amdahl.arm-cool_vs_arm-pip.") if name.endswith(".predicted_speedup") %}
